# The eighteen are independent repositories, each with its own history. This
# repo is what sits above them: the index, the working instructions, the `cq`
# wrapper and the portfolio generator. Those were tracked by nothing at all
# until this file existed.
#
# Listed by name, with every sibling repo named as it appears. The reasoning
# behind that was wrong in a way worth recording: the plan was that a pattern
# like "*/" would silently swallow a nineteenth project the day it appeared, so
# naming them would force the question. What actually happened on the first new
# repo is the opposite and worse -- `git add -A` recorded derx and sockv as
# gitlinks, a bare commit SHA with no submodule config, which is useless to a
# clone and says nothing about the project.
#
# So the list stays, and t/test_portfolio.py now asserts that this repo holds no
# gitlink at all. Forgetting to add a new sibling here is now a failing test
# rather than a broken commit.
# Not one of the eighteen: an upstream Android fork kept here for convenience.
__pycache__/
bigint/
cc/
cmark/
commitq/
corex/
derx/
dwarfdump/
ed25519/
gitobj/
httpd/
inflate/
jail/
jsonc/
lnk/
mydiff/
notally-molly/
pngc/
prof/
psh/
rx/
seccompc/
sha2/
slab/
sockv/
sqlr/
srcdiff/
tarx/
terminfo/
tlp/
tomlc/
trace/
tzf/
unrepro/
utf8n/
vtparse/
walkv/
wasmi/
xmlc/
zipc/
